  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jamaica is currently considering ratification of Convention No. 190 on violence and harassment.

This initiative will benefit workers, employers and the broader community of Jamaica by strengthening laws and practical measures to prevent, protect from, and provide remedies for, violence and harassment at workplace. The ILO&apos;s collaboration will involve the government (especially the Ministry of Labour and Social Security, the Ministry of Culture, Gender, Entertainment and Sport), the social partners, and other stakeholders to ensure effective implementation and alignment with international labour standards.</narrative>
  </description>
